  "release_invariants": [
    "No production mutation without release planning, exact-head certification, and explicit human authorization.",
    "Every path to production deployment must traverse release_plan -> exact_head_certification -> human_release_authority in that order.",
    "Every path to production recovery must already have traversed production deployment and live certification.",
    "Rollback and rollout plans are candidate-bound evidence and must be certified before human release authorization.",
    "Candidate generation, verification, approval, and production mutation may not collapse into one unreviewed authority context.",
    "A head or base identity change invalidates candidate-bound certification and authorization.",
    "Unresolved release-critical evidence cannot be converted to PASS by synthesis.",
    "Every specialist audit is selected through audit_plan_router and synthesis waits for the selected audit set.",
    "Every edge contract may carry only declared source outputs into declared target inputs.",
    "Deterministic transforms and policy checks may not be replaced by model calls without a documented reason.",
    "Only failed local work is retried while still-fresh independent evidence remains reusable.",
    "Any non-PASS live certification must enter pre-authorized recovery before closure.",
    "Production mutation failures with ambiguous side effects may not be automatically retried.",
    "Every authorized deployment carries a deployment_operation_id derived only by exact_head_certification as SHA-256 over an RFC8785 canonical record of repository, exact base, exact head, target environment, rollout plan, and rollback plan; reasoning nodes may not invent this identity.",
    "Production recovery is a one-shot pre-authorized mutation followed by independent certification; failure escalates rather than looping automatically.",
    "Human release authority consumes an externally recorded durable human_approvals state record bound to exact head, exact base, authorized scope, rollout/rollback references, and deployment_operation_id.",
    "Every node exposing RETRY declares a finite retry_policy whose retryable_failures exactly match RETRY-mapped failures and whose terminal_route is not RETRY.",
    "Every controlled cycle declares a completion test, durable budget reference, and escalation route."
  ]
